{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "07RJ", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4951973f0056c502f0a59fa274eb7e0817d3f651989e0c1f261d7cee85cb3b91", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we collect some facts on immersions.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:15acb537fac6d3f885ff2e50ff84cb483af720b3d44d452bee79c0305d1a1f6d", "unit_id": "tag:07RJ:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "07RJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$Z \\to Y \\to X$", "MATH_0002": "$Z \\to X$", "MATH_0003": "$Z \\to Y$", "MATH_0004": "$Z \\to X$", "MATH_0005": "$Y \\to X$", "MATH_0006": "$Z \\to Y$", "MATH_0007": "$Z \\to X$", "MATH_0008": "$Y \\to X$", "MATH_0009": "$Z \\to Y$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-immersion-permanence}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:81ea74ebecfbc998966ea5b5faef124507d448a451505f989cafd35030719c30", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3b4c899dd6f5b30e8ead1a0170c9ad89a59855a6b14a31402433bf37ab487b37", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be morphisms of schemes.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> If <MATH_0002> is an immersion, then <MATH_0003> is an immersion.\n<STRUCT_0003> If <MATH_0004> is a quasi-compact immersion and <MATH_0005> is\nquasi-separated, then <MATH_0006> is a quasi-compact immersion.\n<STRUCT_0004> If <MATH_0007> is a closed immersion and <MATH_0008> is separated,\nthen <MATH_0009> is a closed immersion.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fcc581bbccb1b78b2943fe3a0f85a9f2af3134b3ff1ea2001910305aa0f6a921", "unit_id": "tag:07RK:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "07RJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nZ \\ar[r] \\ar[rd] & Y \\times_X Z \\ar[r] \\ar[d] & Z \\ar[d] \\\\\n& Y \\ar[r] & X\n}\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$Y \\times_X Z \\to Z$", "MATH_0003": "$Y \\times_X Z \\to Y$", "MATH_0004": "$Z \\to X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-section-immersion}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-base-change-immersion}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-composition-immersion}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2d134a3c38e51f20874d6b5dad80957dd58b373468cea1731b35937d00c7cc70", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:42009a0c11aba58c38f1bf3819efe161258bb2f81cb1663d0cbfbe347fd32cfe", "source_text": "In each case the proof is to contemplate the commutative diagram\n<MATH_0001>\nwhere the composition of the top horizontal arrows is the identity.\nLet us prove (1). The first horizontal arrow is a section of\n<MATH_0002>, whence an immersion by\nSchemes, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nThe arrow <MATH_0003> is a base change of <MATH_0004> hence\nan immersion (Schemes, Lemma <REF_0002>).\nFinally, a composition of immersions is an immersion\n(Schemes, Lemma <REF_0003>). This proves (1).\nThe other two results are proved in exactly the same manner.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:95888d527c0f52481170bb3302e79944669d6731e441e4af9056d561015b40c4", "unit_id": "tag:07RK:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "07RJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$h : Z \\to X$", "MATH_0002": "$h$", "MATH_0003": "$h = i \\circ j$", "MATH_0004": "$j : Z \\to \\overline{Z}$", "MATH_0005": "$i : \\overline{Z} \\to X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-factor-quasi-compact-immersion}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e7a1ecc8c3c371cdac37243ad55d3177d958ea522cd1355f28a3fe527b7ee052", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:af04a67f66656da6a7063f8dd4d7acdfc554519571dbfc9bbb3af0db58ab4d0e", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an immersion.\nIf <MATH_0002> is quasi-compact, then we can factor\n<MATH_0003> with <MATH_0004> an\nopen immersion and <MATH_0005> a closed immersion.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:057039c8c47a6cf3298a1fbf1915c1b51f692b1e23032fdb987cc321efd7eda8", "unit_id": "tag:01QV:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "07RJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$h$", "MATH_0002": "$h_*\\mathcal{O}_Z$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{I} = \\Ker(\\mathcal{O}_X \\to h_*\\mathcal{O}_Z)$", "MATH_0005": "$\\overline{Z} \\subset X$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0007": "$h$", "MATH_0008": "$h = i \\circ j$", "MATH_0009": "$i : \\overline{Z} \\to X$", "MATH_0010": "$j$", "MATH_0011": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0012": "$h$", "MATH_0013": "$Z$", "MATH_0014": "$U$", "MATH_0015": "$\\mathcal{I}|_U$", "MATH_0016": "$Z \\to U$", "MATH_0017": "$Z = \\overline{Z} \\cap U$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-immersions-monomorphisms}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-push-forward-quasi-coherent}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{schemes-section-quasi-coherent}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-closed-immersion-bijection-ideals}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-characterize-closed-subspace}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ed25819fc368019e37d30e522bc1bb1a523c55947d9675a986eb0dc93aaa94bf", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a58d22a3af6200f043ef194a0b27986479e32e182663850e1574e8f148121bf9", "source_text": "Note that <MATH_0001> is quasi-compact and quasi-separated (see\nSchemes, Lemma <REF_0001>).\nHence <MATH_0002> is a quasi-coherent sheaf of <MATH_0003>-modules\nby Schemes, Lemma <REF_0002>.\nThis implies that\n<MATH_0004>\nis a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals, see\nSchemes, Section <REF_0003>.\nLet <MATH_0005> be the closed subscheme corresponding\nto <MATH_0006>, see Lemma <REF_0004>.\nBy Schemes, Lemma <REF_0005>\nthe morphism <MATH_0007> factors as\n<MATH_0008> where <MATH_0009> is the inclusion morphism.\nTo see that <MATH_0010> is an open immersion, choose an open subscheme\n<MATH_0011> such that <MATH_0012> induces a closed immersion of <MATH_0013>\ninto <MATH_0014>. Then it is clear that <MATH_0015> is the\nsheaf of ideals corresponding to the closed immersion <MATH_0016>.\nHence we see that <MATH_0017>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e5f8034de020b86657a5f94505dc30e765e1615a11d30a748899a6a3860a9f86", "unit_id": "tag:01QV:proof"}
